      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t see the bug for some reason, but I\u0027m guessing this is due to the limit of data_len being uint16_t?\n\nIn which case, isn\u0027t the max data len actually 0xFFFF?\n\nSuggest EC_PROTO3_MAX_DATA_LEN as the name in this case, to more clearly indicate which maximum, and that it doesn\u0027t include the host request/response header size.  See EC_PROTO2_MAX_PARAM_SIZE above.\n\nOr is this due to some other limit?  It\u0027s unclear from the implementation in the other files whether this max size includes the request/response header or not.",
